  "why_this_direction": "The reviewed conditional-query construction needs one immutable original coordinate definition before numerical functions or changed traces can be measured. The native graph and source-bound causal loader are fixture-tested. Bind their population and domain without importing any withdrawn state-value objective.",
  "repeating_pattern_check": "Previous readings followed tokens, pooled distinct reference observations, normalized surviving support, or treated native metadata as qualification. This definition takes only the original fitting inventory, keeps raw computational paths and each mapped event, and explicitly contains no numerical functions or native-qualification claim.",
  "hypothesis": "Common original native-sized query probes and distinct original conditional functions provide an experimental coordinate domain in which recurring computational differences may be tested; this compilation tests only whether all required original coordinates and sources can be bound completely.",
  "what_went_wrong_before": "State-value and same-token objectives did not measure shared calculation. The historical success-set artifact supplies original membership and computational paths only, never its withdrawn targets or scalar readings.",
  "rule": "All original fitting successes are axes and probes; every original raw mapped event is separate, duplicate path entries count once. Each success has equal probe mass split over its mapped events. Witnesses exclude axis and recipient identities. Use saved directional paths only, no symmetric union, no token-selected support, no current model, no averaging mapped reference functions.",
  "prediction": "A complete source-bound coordinate definition is produced for every original successful question and answer event at every model merge, retaining all fitting recipients and prompts solely for acquisition identity.",
  "would_weaken_it": "Missing sources, incompatible model or row identities, incomplete computational paths, or omission of an original success prevents compilation. Completion alone says nothing about discrimination, native context reconstruction, improvement or closure.",
